%
% WHAT THIS SHEET IS -- AND IS NOT (the founder's rule, kept):
% This notation covers EXACTLY what the house engine composed
% and struck: the rhythmic spine (resonance.studio.spine),
% the composed violin arpeggio (resonance.studio.arpeggio),
% and the Sigma binaural ground (resonance.binaural). The
% MusicGen bed is NOT transcribed here: its transcription is
% a separate production, still owed, and no sheet for it has
% been fabricated. What the bed WAS told, in every section,
% stands below as the motif: the same repeating four-note F minor piano motif (F, A-flat, C, A-flat)
%
% THE GRID: 137 BPM, 48 kHz. One bar = 84,087.59 samples of float truth;
% the program is bars_to_samples(120) = 10,090,511 samples = 210.219 s, one rounding at
% the total. Swing 0.12 on spine and dancer alike. Stitch
% crossfades are 2 WHOLE BARS each, on bar lines.
%
% SECTION CHART (spine truth; modes = the arpeggio's realization):
%   intro     bars   1-  8  sparse   arp:statement     0:00.0 - 0:14.0
%   hook      bars   9- 16  full     arp:runs          0:14.0 - 0:28.0
%   verse1    bars  17- 32  driving  arp:bariolage     0:28.0 - 0:56.1
%   hook      bars  33- 40  full     arp:runs          0:56.1 - 1:10.1
%   feature   bars  41- 56  open     arp:runs          1:10.1 - 1:38.1
%   hook      bars  57- 64  full     arp:runs          1:38.1 - 1:52.1
%   verse2    bars  65- 80  driving  arp:bariolage     1:52.1 - 2:20.1
%   hook      bars  81- 88  full     arp:runs          2:20.1 - 2:34.2
%   verse3    bars  89-104  driving  arp:bariolage16   2:34.2 - 3:02.2
%   hook_out  bars 105-112  full     arp:runs          3:02.2 - 3:16.2
%   outro     bars 113-120  sparse   arp:statement_fade 3:16.2 - 3:30.2
%
% DRUM PATTERNS -- one bar of 16 steps per density (see spine.py):
% FULL (hook): kick 1 . . . . . x . 1 . x . . . x . ; clap 5,13;
%   closed hats on the 8ths, open hat step 15 odd bars; 808 1(6) 7(2) 9(6).
% DRIVING (verse): kick 1, 9, 11 (ghost 16 odd bars); snare 5,13;
%   hats all 16 steps; 808 1(4) 4(1) 7(2) 9(4) 11(2) 13(3).
% OPEN (feature): kick 1, 9; snare 5,13; hats on 8ths; 808 1(8) 9(6) long.
% SPARSE (intro/outro): kick 1; hats 1, 9 (5, 13 from bar 3); 808 1(12) held.
% FILL (last bar of full/driving): snare walks 13-16, .5/.65/.8/1.0.
% THE 808 MOVEMENT: F - Db - Ab - Eb (i - VI - III - VII), roots
% MIDI 29 / 37 / 32 / 39, restarting at the tonic each section.
F,,4|Db,4|Ab,,4|Eb,4|]
%
% THE ARPEGGIO -- the dancer. Composed from the SOLFEGGIO LADDER,
% played at its equal-tempered staff approximations; each carrier's
% cents offset from its staff pitch is stated, never smoothed:
%   UT      396 Hz -> G   (MIDI 67, 392.0 Hz) +17.6 cents
%   RE      417 Hz -> ^G  (MIDI 68, 415.3 Hz) +7.1 cents
%   MI      528 Hz -> c   (MIDI 72, 523.25 Hz) +15.6 cents
%   FA      639 Hz -> _e  (MIDI 75, 622.25 Hz) +46.0 cents
%   SOL     741 Hz -> ^f  (MIDI 78, 739.99 Hz) +2.4 cents
%   LA      852 Hz -> ^g  (MIDI 80, 830.61 Hz) +44.0 cents
% Phrasing is Fibonacci -- phrase lengths 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 climbing
% the ladder cyclically. THE FIGURE (one cell, 20 notes, L:1/16):
G ^G c _e ^f ^g G ^G c _e ^f ^g G ^G c _e ^f ^g G ^G |
% Phrase map: [1] G | [1] ^G | [2] c _e | [3] ^f ^g G |
%   [5] ^G c _e ^f ^g | [8] G ^G c _e ^f ^g G ^G
% REALIZATIONS: RUNS = the cell tiled at 16ths, phrase heads
% accented. BARIOLAGE = at 8ths, cell notes alternate with the
% pedal c (MI, the open string). One full bariolage cell (L:1/8):
G c ^G c c c _e c ^f c ^g c G c ^G c c c _e c ^f c ^g c G c ^G c c c _e c ^f c ^g c G c ^G c |
% BARIOLAGE16 = the same alternation at 16ths (verse3, the biggest
% chair). STATEMENT = the figure at 8th spacing, phrase-final notes
% held two extra steps, passes repeated; the outro's statement fades.
% TOTAL ARPEGGIO NOTES AS STRUCK: 1504 (per section: intro=48, hook=128, verse1=128, hook=128, feature=256, hook=128, verse2=128, hook=128, verse3=256, hook_out=128, outro=48).
% The contour is humanized (micro-drift + vibrato, Tools Wing) and
% the layer orbits at 0.03 Hz, mixed at -9.0 dB under the standing mix's RMS.
%
% THE SIGMA GROUND: carriers intended 200.0 / 213.0 Hz, MEASURED on the struck sigma.wav:
% 200.0 / 213.0 Hz, separation 13.0 Hz, at -28.0 dB under the bed's RMS.
% MASTER: -15.02 LUFS after (target -14.0), true peak -1.02 dBTP, ceiling overrode loudness: True.
% STEREO LAW: bed correlation 1.0 -> 0.9364, low band 1.0, master correlation 0.8865, side -28.3 dBFS.
%
% 93 -- Live, Love, and let Love, Live.
